sts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdougbrown/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdougbrown/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdougbrown/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdougbrown/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdougbrown/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdougbrown/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdougbrown/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-24T13:46:52Z","updated_at":"2026-10-24T13:46:52Z","body":"`👾 AI Agent` Round summary for head cbcf58d.\n\n**Restack.** The branch is rebased onto pr/06-plan-chain 77d23f0 and has no merge commits. The old \"address umpire findings\" merges carried real fixes; they are now ordinary commits 03ffc2f and 31f38e8, and the 12 earlier thread replies were re-pointed to those SHAs. 45fb6d1 uses the `initcfg` policy-name constants.\n\n**Fixes this round**\n- a6d0f3d: `paddock plan` fails when the home directory is unknown. 851e37a: `CacheDir` refuses a home that is not absolute and keys on the exact spec ref.\n- aedcce8: the file-workspace error case now fails without the `IsDir` check.\n- 8cbda1a, d8598a6, fddffbc: the `cache_key` file must resolve to a regular file inside the workdir. It is opened through an `os.Root` without blocking, and at most 64 MiB is read. A symlink to `/dev/zero` or a FIFO used to hang `paddock plan --phase setup`, and a link out of the workdir hashed host files into the plan. Local review found this.\n- a541f51: an allowlist whose egress sets define no hosts is an error. paddock-init would have rejected that plan.\n- ea4a22d, 022632a: `claude.skills` and `claude.agents` must lie in a read-only mount with no symlink between the mount and the path. Before, a link inside a read-only mount could lead into the writable workspace.\n- 2a34616: AGENTS.md names the setup cache as the one rw mount a spec can cause, and SECURITY.md residual risk 7 covers the cache shared between workspaces.\n- cbcf58d: every `PrepareSetupCache` error in the tests is checked.\n\n**Body findings, rounds 1 and 2 (`internal/resolve/chain.go:107` and `:124`): reject `setup.cache_dir`/`cache_key` from repository-trust specs in `checkSpec`.** Not enforced in this PR.\n- No `SpecSource` returns repository-trust specs in v1, so nothing reaches this path today.\n- SECURITY.md residual risk 6 already lists these fields among those `checkSpec` must reject before repository specs load.\n- The paddock plan's project-spec table gives project specs a setup command and its cache key, which conflicts with residual risk 6. #6 raised that conflict for the owner to decide. Enforcing one side here would pre-empt that decision.\n- `checkSpec` is a #6 function. The owner's decision belongs there or in the PR that adds a repository `SpecSource`.\n\n**Left for the owner:** whether the setup cache stays shared across workspaces (residual risk 7; umpire `cache.go:29`), and the repository-spec trust model above.\n\nChecks on cbcf58d: `make build build-init vet fmtcheck test` and `go test -race -count=1 ./...` pass on macOS and in `golang:1.26` on Linux. All 15 review threads are answered and resolved.\n","author_association":"OWNER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdougbrown/paddock/issues/comments/6384977328/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdougbrown/paddock/issues/comments/6384978500","html_url":"https://github.com/sdougbrown/paddock/pull/7#issuecomment-6384978500","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdougbrown/paddock/issues/7","id":6384978500,"node_id":"IC_kwDOVTwlwc8AAAABfJMKRA","user":{"login":"sdougbrown","id":2266707,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNjY3MDc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22